WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.110 --> 00:00:04.110
This is the story of Robert Smalls.

00:00:05.030 --> 00:00:09.500
A man who was born a slave and went on to hold one of the highest positions in government, 

00:00:09.700 --> 00:00:12.190
and become a hero of the Civil War.

00:00:14.030 --> 00:00:16.630
Robert Smalls was born into slavery in South Carolina.

00:00:17.100 --> 00:00:21.770
Back then, if a slave had enough money they could literally buy their freedom.

00:00:22.040 --> 00:00:24.230
But Smalls wanted to buy the freedom of his whole family,

00:00:25.060 --> 00:00:27.490
a price that was more than he could afford.

00:00:28.000 --> 00:00:31.160
In 1862, while working close to northern lines,

00:00:31.200 --> 00:00:34.120
on a Confederate boat called the CSS Planter,

00:00:34.190 --> 00:00:36.170
Smalls hatched a plan.

00:00:37.230 --> 00:00:40.190
One night, when the white officers left the ship,

00:00:40.200 --> 00:00:42.160
Smalls was left in charge.

00:00:43.170 --> 00:00:45.070
With no time to spare,

00:00:45.060 --> 00:00:51.060
Smalls took over the ship, rounded up the other slaves and their families, and set sail towards union waters.

00:00:51.200 --> 00:00:56.200
But Smalls and his crew would have to pass through four Confederate checkpoints before they would be free.

00:00:57.200 --> 00:01:04.110
Smalls disguised himself by wearing the captain's jacket and straw hat, and mimicking his gait.

00:01:06.040 --> 00:01:08.130
Having worked on the CSS Planter for years,

00:01:08.220 --> 00:01:13.020
he knew all of the hand signals used by Confederate sailors to pass through checkpoints.

00:01:14.090 --> 00:01:18.040
The boat passed one, two and three checkpoints.

00:01:19.170 --> 00:01:25.210
At the final point, which was also the most heavily armed, Smalls flashed a signal and got the go-ahead.

00:01:28.010 --> 00:01:33.020
And just like that, Robert Smalls and his family literally sailed to freedom.

00:01:33.180 --> 00:01:38.010
Towards the end of his life, Smalls returned to the house in which he was born a slave,

00:01:38.050 --> 00:01:42.020
buying it outright from his former slave master to live out his days.

00:01:43.030 --> 00:01:47.230
A man who went from slave to one of the most prominent figures in America.

